>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"}; open simpLib;
## `remove_solver`

``` hol4
simpLib.remove_solver : string -> simpset -> simpset
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Removes a named solver from a simpset.

`remove_solver name ss` removes every entry called `name` from both the
safe and unsafe solver lists of `ss`. If neither list contains `name`,
the simpset is returned unchanged and no warning is issued.

This operation is persistent on the returned simpset. To suppress a
named solver only for one simplifier invocation, pass `Excl name` in
that invocation's theorem list.

### Failure

Never fails.

### Example

``` hol4
val ss_without_arithmetic =
  simpLib.remove_solver "linear arithmetic" ss;
```

### See also

[`simpLib.add_unsafe_solver`](#simpLib.add_unsafe_solver),
[`simpLib.add_safe_solver`](#simpLib.add_safe_solver),
[`simpLib.set_unsafe_solvers`](#simpLib.set_unsafe_solvers),
[`simpLib.set_safe_solvers`](#simpLib.set_safe_solvers)
